title: 'CI: Improve zombienet stability'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Five small things bundled here:

    1. Download of the binaries in `.github/zombienet-tests/zombienet_polkadot_tests.yml` could fail because of some connection reset during download that was not covered by the current `--retry` flag. Now retries on all errors.
    2. Update zombienet to 0.4.16 to get [560](https://github.com/paritytech/zombienet-sdk/pull/560)
    3. My tip sync zombienet was sometimes stumbling because the relay chain side was slow syncing. Now uses --relay-chain-rpc URL directly.
    4. Raised the tip sync test's gap-window finality timeout from 1200s to 2400s. CI logs show the wait takes ~1210-1260s on a healthy network (the parachain finalizes one block per ~12.5s), so the old timeout was a coin flip and the top cause of merge-queue evictions this week.
    5. The tip sync DB generator added the passive `pruned-node` via `with_collator(...).validator(false)`, but `with_collator` force-sets `validator(true)` after the closure, so the node was enrolled as a second genesis Aura authority. The tip-sync network only runs `collator-1`, so that phantom authority owned half the Aura slots with no producer, halving finality throughput (~12.5s/block instead of ~6s) and driving the flakiness in item 4. Switched it to `with_fullnode(...)` so the snapshot's authority set is `collator-1` only. NOTE: requires regenerating and re-uploading the storage-chain fixture bundle before it takes effect.
crates:
- name: sp-weights
  bump: patch
- name: sc-rpc-spec-v2
  bump: patch
- name: staging-xcm
  bump: patch
